{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`next_batch` returns a ticket as available for work while `ticket_deps` reports that same\nticket has open blockers and `ready_to_work: false`. The two readiness answers disagree, and\n`next_batch` is the one agents are told to use to pick work, so an agent following it can\nclaim a ticket whose prerequisites have not landed.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 on the live store, epic `spin-cub-usher` (`65dd-e93b-666a-4caa`).\n\nThe epic's ADR child `eaved-lighted-hedgehog` (`a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87`) was linked with two\nprerequisite edges recorded from the prerequisite side:\n\n```\nlink modern-loathful-snake        eaved-lighted-hedgehog blocks\nlink divinatory-offensive-groundhog eaved-lighted-hedgehog blocks\n```\n\nBoth prerequisites are open. Then:\n\n- `ticket_deps eaved-lighted-hedgehog` returns\n  `{\"deps\": [], \"blockers\": [\"1cef-7fbc-e402-467c\", \"5169-ab69-9c23-4f8b\"], \"ready_to_work\": false}`\n- `next_batch spin-cub-usher` returns that same `a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87` inside `batch`, with\n  `available_pool: 2`, and does not list it under any `skipped_*` key.\n\nExpected: a ticket with an open blocker is excluded from `batch` (it belongs in a skipped\nbucket). Actual: it is offered as available work.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py` derives readiness solely from a ticket's OUTGOING\n`depends_on` relations. At `next_batch.py:176-182` it builds `open_depends_on` by filtering\nthat ticket's own `deps` for `relation == \"depends_on\"` and skips the ticket only when that\nlist is non-empty; the blocked-id set at `next_batch.py:220-228` applies the same\noutgoing-`depends_on` test.\n\nA `blocks` edge recorded from the prerequisite (`A blocks B`) leaves B with an INBOUND edge\nand no outgoing `depends_on`, so B passes both filters. `ticket_deps` computes `blockers`\nfrom the inbound direction and therefore disagrees.\n\nThis matters because both link directions are sanctioned: `AGENTS.md` documents `blocks` and\n`depends_on` as two of the canonical relations, and the brainstorm/authoring guidance tells\nauthors to \"record their parent and prerequisite relationships with `blocks` or\n`depends_on`\". Only one of those two spellings is honored by the scheduler.\n\n## Scope\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py` readiness derivation, plus its tests. The fix is to\ntreat an open inbound `blocks` edge as blocking, exactly as `ticket_deps` already does — not\nto change the link vocabulary or the recorded edges.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing `ticket_deps`, which is the surface that already answers correctly.\n- Altering blocking-link promotion or the link relation vocabulary.\n- Reworking the file-impact conflict scheduling in the same module.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nBehavior-narrowing: tickets that were previously offered while blocked stop being offered.\nNo stored data or event shape changes, so back-out is reverting the readiness predicate.\nAny consumer relying on the current over-permissive batch would have been scheduling\nunclaimable work.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests against the real `next_batch_state` over a temporary store seeded with a\nprerequisite pair, covering both edge spellings and the symmetry with `ticket_deps`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A ticket whose only prerequisite edge is an inbound `blocks` from an OPEN ticket is\n      absent from `batch` and present in a skipped bucket; verified by `pytest` over a\n      seeded temporary store asserting the returned `batch` ids.\n- [x] The same ticket becomes available once that prerequisite closes; verified by `pytest`\n      asserting it appears in `batch` after the blocker transitions to closed.\n- [x] `next_batch` and `ticket_deps` agree for every child of a seeded epic: no id appears in\n      `batch` while `ticket_deps` reports `ready_to_work: false`; verified by `pytest`\n      asserting the intersection is empty.\n- [x] The existing outgoing-`depends_on` behavior is unchanged; verified by `pytest` over a\n      seeded pair using `depends_on`, asserting the same exclusion as before.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` pass; the live reproduction above no longer\noffers `a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87` while its blockers are open."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788365292917911001,"uuid":"fd6ed29f-229d-4dfb-b838-8cdcddbad1a3"}